  "notes": "This verb almost always appears in fixed patterns rather than being used freely.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜を{介|かい}して (through ~, via ~) — sense 1\n- 〜を{介|かい}する (to go through ~) — sense 1\n- {意|い}に{介|かい}さない (not to care about, not to be bothered by) — sense 2\n\nSense 1 is formal and commonly appears in written language, news, and business contexts. {通|つう}じて (through) is a more casual alternative.\n\nSense 2 almost exclusively appears in the set phrase {意|い}に{介|かい}さない / {意|い}に{介|かい}する. The affirmative {意|い}に{介|かい}する is rare; the negative form is far more common.",
